title: >-
  Missing Is Not Zero: Well-Posed Modality Removal, and What It Reveals About
  RGB-D Segmentation Robustness
abstract: >-
  Multimodal semantic segmentation is evaluated for robustness to missing
  modalities under a protocol that sets the absent modality's input to zero.
  This work shows that protocol is not architecture-neutral, states a
  removal-equivalence criterion separating an input sentinel from a named
  model-level removal, and gives an inference-time test for it that requires no
  retraining. Applied to an architecture whose depth pathway admits an exact
  neutral element, it partitions a missing-depth gap against a same-capacity
  reference and compares the modality-complete cost of three training recipes.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/CrepuscularIRIS/ugra-rgbd-robust
keywords:
  - RGB-D semantic segmentation
  - missing modality
  - multimodal robustness
  - model diagnostics
  - relational-bias attention

